<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Testing on Kunal Kushwaha</title><link>https://kunalkushwaha.github.io/tags/testing/</link><description>Recent content in Testing on Kunal Kushwaha</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0900</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://kunalkushwaha.github.io/tags/testing/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Before I Trust an Agent, I Try to Break Its Box</title><link>https://kunalkushwaha.github.io/2026/11/06/before-i-trust-an-agent/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0900</pubDate><guid>https://kunalkushwaha.github.io/2026/11/06/before-i-trust-an-agent/</guid><description>&lt;div class="note"&gt;&lt;span class="note-label"&gt;Updated 15 November 2026 for 0.1.0-rc.3&lt;/span&gt;The results below were recorded in October 2026 on Koala&amp;rsquo;s preview builds. See &lt;a href="#what-changed-in-rc3"&gt;What changed in rc.3&lt;/a&gt; near the end.&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;figure&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="fig-card"&gt;&lt;img src="hero.jpg" alt="Untrusted code runs inside the VM. The host stays outside the guest boundary." loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;figcaption&gt;Untrusted code runs inside the VM. The host stays outside the guest boundary.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In October I wrote that Koala should &lt;a href="https://kunalkushwaha.github.io/2026/10/17/give-every-agent-its-own-room/"&gt;give every agent its own room&lt;/a&gt;: one Linux VM per workload, with the network check and the credentials kept on the host. That is a design claim. Claims are cheap.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>